<title>UK: Next eases on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Next eases on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Next Plc eased on profit-taking after December UK retails sales figures disappointed investors, market makers said.</p>
<p>At 1604 GMT, the shares were down 10p to 559.</p>
<p>Others in the sector also fell. Among them, shares in Kingfisher Plc dropped 9p to 663-1/2, while shares in Dixon Group slipped 4-1/2p to 508-1/2. Shares in Marks &amp; Spencer fell 5-1/2p to 487.  </p>
<p>Next shares have had a bit of a bounce last week and this morning's set of figures, showing a 0.8 percent decline in December sales month-on-month, &quot;were not encouraging and got people nervous,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
